"""Belleau Wood: the Marne, 6 June 1918.  A sample game for the
Grognard engine.

The German spring offensive has reached the Marne, forty miles from
Paris.  The 4th Marine Brigade has stopped it at Lucy-le-Bocage, and on
6 June it attacks: Hill 142 at dawn, and in the evening Belleau Wood
itself and the village of Bouresches, across open wheat swept by
machine guns hidden among the rocks.  Play either side against the
computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./belleau (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.belleau.json.  ./belleau --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

